From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Date: Sun, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: square both terms of the N-PHY RSSI VCM search

The narrowband RSSI calibration picks, out of eight VCM settings, the one
whose polled I and Q results are closest to zero. The distance it minimises
is meant to be I^2 + Q^2, and b43 computes

	currd = results[vcm][i] * results[vcm][i] +
		results[vcm][i + 1] * results[vcm][i];

so the second term is Q*I, not Q*Q. The reference squares both:

	curr_d = poll_results[vcm][result_idx] * poll_results[vcm][result_idx] +
		 poll_results[vcm][result_idx + 1] *
		 poll_results[vcm][result_idx + 1];

Q*I is not a distance. It is negative whenever the two rails have opposite
signs, which is most of the sweep, so the minimum lands wherever that
product happens to be most negative rather than where the pair is smallest.
The calibration then programs that VCM and derives the fine digital offsets
from its results, so a wrong pick costs both.

Measured on an MMIO capture of wl 6.30.102.7 on a BCM6362, N-PHY rev 8 with
radio 2057 rev 8: with the term squared the port picks VCM 2 for core 0,
which is what the vendor driver picks, and the two narrowband offsets that
follow come out identical to the capture as well. Without it the port picks
3. The second RSSI calibration of an interface coming up goes from 623 to
956 matched operations out of 960, and from 22 contiguous blocks to 3.

Not tested on hardware.

Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n22476
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/HEAD/router-data/dsl-3580l/opinit-ch1-ch6-bw20.decoded

The selection for core 0 and the two offsets it decides are records #22953
to #22958 of that capture:

  53677.051000 #22953    cpu0 RAD.MOD  addr=0x00b4 val=0x0002 mask=0x0007

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -2166,7 +2166,7 @@ static void b43_nphy_rev3_rssi_cal(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 				continue;
 			for (vcm = 0; vcm < 8; vcm++) {
 				currd = results[vcm][i] * results[vcm][i] +
-					results[vcm][i + 1] * results[vcm][i];
+					results[vcm][i + 1] * results[vcm][i + 1];
 				if (currd < mind) {
 					mind = currd;
 					minvcm = vcm;
